{"assets":["/statement-assets/e91edf89f2cec5401aa756758ad4efc6916622674560a98ea91ef2c4f4bd35ea.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"553","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Nudist Beach"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Nudist Beach is planning a military operation to attack the Life Fibers. In this operation, they will attack and capture several cities which are currently under the control of the Life Fibers."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" cities, labeled from 1 to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":", and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" bidirectional roads between them. Currently, there are Life Fibers in every city. In addition, there are "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" cities that are fortresses of the Life Fibers that cannot be captured under any circumstances. So, the Nudist Beach can capture an arbitrary non-empty subset of cities with no fortresses."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After the operation, Nudist Beach will have to defend the captured cities from counterattack. If they capture a city and it is connected to many Life Fiber controlled cities, it will be easily defeated. So, Nudist Beach would like to capture a set of cities such that for each captured city the ratio of Nudist Beach controlled neighbors among all neighbors of that city is as high as possible. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"More formally, they would like to capture a non-empty set of cities "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":" with no fortresses of Life Fibers. The strength of a city "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/e91edf89f2cec5401aa756758ad4efc6916622674560a98ea91ef2c4f4bd35ea.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" is defined as (number of neighbors of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" in "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":") / (total number of neighbors of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Here, two cities are called neighbors if they are connnected with a road. The goal is to maximize the strength of the weakest city in "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Given a description of the graph, and the cities with fortresses, find a non-empty subset that maximizes the strength of the weakest city. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of input contains three integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n, m, k"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2  ≤  n  ≤ 100 000"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ m ≤ 100 000"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ k ≤ n - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of input contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers, representing the cities with fortresses. These cities will all be distinct. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contain the roads. The "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th of these lines will have 2 integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai, bi"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ ai, bi ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai ≠ bi"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Every city will have at least one road adjacent to it."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There is no more than one road between each pair of the cities."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line should contain an integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"r"},{"kind":"text","text":", denoting the size of an optimum set ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ r ≤ n - k"},{"kind":"text","text":"). "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line should contain "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"r"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers, denoting the cities in the set. Cities may follow in an arbitrary order. This line should not contain any of the cities with fortresses."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If there are multiple possible answers, print any of them."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"9 8 4\n3 9 6 8\n1 2\n1 3\n1 4\n1 5\n2 6\n2 7\n2 8\n2 9\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n1 4 5\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"10 8 2\n2 9\n1 3\n2 9\n4 5\n5 6\n6 7\n7 8\n8 10\n10 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"8\n1 5 4 8 10 6 3 7\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first example case achieves a strength of 1/2. No other subset is strictly better."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second example case achieves a strength of 1. Note that the subset doesn't necessarily have to be connected."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"553D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/553/problem/D"}